[NC_013] FALSIFIED
  claim:    A phase lead is fixed only modulo the forcing period, and is not measurable at all against a channel that does not move.
            forcing period 40 samples at 100 Hz
            lead of zero periods: +0.0000 s
            lead of one period:   +0.0000 s   <- indistinguishable
            constructed LAG of 4 samples: raw search returns -4, wrapped to -4
              the raw branch is chosen by where the search lands. When this row
              was first run the SIGN of that lead was what the agreement check
              read, so the branch was deciding a verdict. Leads are reported in
              the principal branch (-P/2, +P/2] and, from 2026-09-27, the phase
              is read by NO verdict: source() decides on amplitude checked
              against ONSET timing (NC_022) and its return carries no phase.
            near half a period: sign_determined=False -- the sign is withheld, not reported
            fixture F1 (A bursts, B quiet): SOURCE_A_MODE, decided by amplitude_ratio, checked against onset timing; phase diagnostic on the same traces: NOT_EVALUABLE
              a phase lead against a channel that does not move is a property
              of its residual variation (NC_012).

[NC_022] HOLDS
  claim:    With A leading by exactly one forcing period, onset timing classifies the source and the phase diagnostic reads zero.
            F4: body A bursts at sample 100, body B at sample 140, one forcing
            period (40 samples) later. Amplitude ratio 7.189390071142242.
            verdict: SOURCE_A_MODE   decided by: amplitude_ratio, checked against onset timing
            onset lead of A over B: +40.0 samples (+0.400 s), onset agrees: True
            phase DIAGNOSTIC on the same traces: +0.0 samples in the principal branch
              one period and zero are the same peak to a periodic correlation,
              so phase reads A as not leading. Onset reads the period. The
              worked instance predicts a lead of about one period, which is
              exactly the value a phase reading cannot resolve.

